---
title: "What a launched analysis actually does"
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor dev as Developer
    participant ui as Launcher
    participant api as POST /api/analyses
    participant db as SQLite
    participant worker as AnalysisWorker
    participant src as Source
    participant engine as perf-sentinel

    dev->>ui: fills the form
    ui->>api: submit
    Note over api: validated against the source kind<br/>before anything is queued, so an<br/>impossible pair is refused now
    api->>db: insert run, pending
    api-->>ui: 202 Accepted, Location: /api/analyses/id

    loop every second while idle
        worker->>db: TryClaimNextRunAsync
    end
    db-->>worker: pending becomes running

    alt source is a daemon
        worker->>src: GET api/export/report
        src-->>worker: report JSON
    else source is a trace backend
        worker->>engine: spawn, tempo or jaeger-query
        Note over worker,engine: the auth header travels as an<br/>environment variable, never on argv
        engine->>src: queries the backend
        engine-->>worker: report JSON on stdout
    end

    worker->>engine: spawn, report --input --output
    Note over worker,engine: a second spawn because only report<br/>writes HTML, cwd is the report directory
    engine-->>worker: id.html written
    worker->>db: succeeded

    ui->>api: GET /api/analyses/id
    api-->>ui: succeeded
    ui->>dev: iframe over /reports/id.html
